    "One draw is one closure pattern. Treat spread across --site-seed values as a range, not a confidence interval.",
    "Closures are edge-level and permanent once active: no partial capacity, no reopening, no contraflow, no detour signage.",
    "The arterial pool is uniform over qualifying named streets in the demand bounding box, which is NOT uniform over demand: the box is several times the area of the demand footprint, so draws land disproportionately in the periphery (same caveat as build_scenario_crandom_2026.py). 25 of 38 arterials fell inside the p05-p95 demand core in this draw. Restricting the pool to the primary demand component removes the wrong-component no-ops but does not make the draw demand-weighted.",
